{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546368-boiling-blood-and-baali","id":1546368,"title":"Boiling Blood and Baali","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-24T21:09:11-08:00","id":1546368,"title":"Boiling Blood and Baali","content":"So, I know that's a weird question, but I was having this discussion with some friends of mine.<br /> So, let's imagine a Baali with Daimoinon 6 and immunity to fire (one could also get this as advantage/infeernal pact, etc). In your opinion, would this cainite be affected by Thaumaturgy Rego Vitae lv 5 Blood Boil? There are some arguments that say no, because &quot;boiling would be related to burning, therefore fire and so it makes no sense for it to affect the cainite&quot; while others say that &quot;fire is one thing, having your blood mystically boiled to destroy you from the inside isn't related to fire per se&quot;. <br /> <br /> To be honest, I'm still in doubt about these two opinions and I'd love to see other opinions on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T23:00:44-08:00","id":1546371,"title":"","content":"I would say yes<br /> Boiling is not releted to fire but heat; boiling to heat something until it starts to produce bubbles and steam<br /> While it is categorised as &quot;burn&quot; it is not caused by fire. Ice could burn you too for example - I know it is a figure of speech but the sympthoms are quite similar if not same. The water in the skin cells freezes, forming sharp ice crystals that can damage the skin and muascle cell structure.<br /> The comination of heat, steam, bubbles, sudden internal pressure change is what damages and destroyes the tissue and cells, not the fire itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T23:27:43-08:00","id":1546372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546368-boiling-blood-and-baali?p=1546371#post1546371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say yes<br /> Boiling is not releted to fire but heat; boiling to heat something until it starts to produce bubbles and steam<br /> While it is categorised as &quot;burn&quot; it is not caused by fire. Ice could burn you too for example - I know it is a figure of speech but the sympthoms are quite similar if not same. The water in the skin cells freezes, forming sharp ice crystals that can damage the skin and muascle cell structure.<br /> The comination of heat, steam, bubbles, sudden internal pressure change is what damages and destroyes the tissue and cells, not the fire itself</div> </div> </div> </div>Your point is very good. Especially because we're talking about magic here, your comparissons are also good, not to mention that making Fire Immunity even more op than it already is, is problematic in my view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-24T23:59:40-08:00","id":1546373,"title":"","content":"I think a better question would be, does the level 2 Blood Rage affect a D6 Fire Immunity user? The Path of Blood powers operate by usurping control over vitae of another, so rather than a Flame burning a vampire and thus boiling their blood, the path power allows the Thaumaturge to tell the victims blood to self-destruct rather than being spent. <br /> <br /> If this causes a problem, then just have the power do half damage to the target. Thus you don't invalidate either ability purchase and maintain balance. Though if the Thaumaturge tried to use Lure of Flames, the D6 Fire Immunity would win the rock/paper/scissors match and take no damage.<br /> <br /> Where this gets interesting is with secondary damage from using fire. For instance, if you launch a fire ball at a D6 Fire Immune vampire, they would be unharmed by it. But if that fire detonates the gas tank of a car next to them, they can still take damage from the concussive force, shrapnel, or just the wreck of the vehicle landing on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T06:11:18-08:00","id":1546380,"title":"","content":"The blood boils, but the heat doesn\u2019t damage the Baali. It inflicts lethal instead of aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T16:49:06-08:00","id":1546412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546368-boiling-blood-and-baali?p=1546380#post1546380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The blood boils, but the heat doesn\u2019t damage the Baali. It inflicts lethal instead of aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>That, alongside the idea of making it deal half damage, seem like good choices. I think Fire Immunity to a vampire need to be dealt with care, otherwise it becomes perhaps too powerful as fire and its possible variations are so dominant in the WoD (many years ago I remember I made a post in this forum about the &quot;strange lack of powers relating to ice and cold, especially in vampire).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T19:10:40-08:00","id":1546415,"title":"","content":"My take is that fire immunity is fire immunity: no connection to heat or other materials, hence blood boiling works normally. Otherwise, one could also argue that sunlight <i>burns</i> vampires and should be excluded as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T21:36:02-08:00","id":1546418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546368-boiling-blood-and-baali?p=1546415#post1546415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take is that fire immunity is fire immunity: no connection to heat or other materials, hence blood boiling works normally. Otherwise, one could also argue that sunlight <i>burns</i> vampires and should be excluded as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's in fact a very good observation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T21:41:45-08:00","id":1546419,"title":"","content":"Though how does fire damage? It largely damaged through heat. If you\u2019re doused with flaming gasoline, your skin gets hot and us damaged by that heat. If you are in a burning building, the rooms will be very hot regardless of flames touching your body. Do Baali take damage from the heat if all of the fires that they are exposed to?<br /> <br /> Daimoinon is a rare Discipline and level 6 is an elder power, it should be strikingly effective, including against boiling blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T23:07:32-08:00","id":1546422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1546368-boiling-blood-and-baali?p=1546419#post1546419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though how does fire damage? It largely damaged through heat. If you\u2019re doused with flaming gasoline, your skin gets hot and us damaged by that heat. If you are in a burning building, the rooms will be very hot regardless of flames touching your body. Do Baali take damage from the heat if all of the fires that they are exposed to?<br /> <br /> Daimoinon is a rare Discipline and level 6 is an elder power, it should be strikingly effective, including against boiling blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot check the book now, but to my memory VDA20 has a section on damage from extreme heat and extreme cold, which is distinct from fire damage. Also, fire does aggravated damage to vampires because it's a bane for them, not because of the natural and physical way it works; their body reacts differently to the touch of fire than a corpse normally would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-25T23:07:51-08:00","id":1546423,"title":"","content":"Fire hurt vampires because of the Curse of an Archangle (okay fire also burns humans but it consumes vampires like dry paper) - on the metaphisical level<br /> On the physical level Fire is the rapid oxidation of a material (the fuel) in the exothermic chemical process of combustion, releasing heat, light, and various reaction products.<br /> Boiling works similar but different ways<br /> D6 would not give a protection in my opinion against boiling or any not-fire related damage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-26T17:37:41-08:00","id":1546435,"title":"","content":"At least until some smartass alchemist Tremere loads a syringe of aluminum powder suspended in mineral oil, and injects that into a target's veins prior to using cauldron of blood <i>[y'all can figure out the implications of that]</i>...<br /> <br /> I'd rule the damage downgrades to either bashing or lethal, depending on circumstances and mood.<br /> <br /> It's important to note Daimoinon 6, depending on edition and write-up, isn't an absolute immunity from anything that might be defined as &quot;fire&quot;. That's limited to fringe supernatural use cases, like horrid reality which paradoxically bypasses the immunity (though I'd absolutely grant a difficulty bonus to the disbelief rolls). Balefire and (true) hellfire bypass it as well, if I remember correctly, because they don't merely damage the flesh but the soul's connection to it. The Thaumaturgy ritual burning blade bypasses it as well, as that's a &quot;generic&quot; magic effect that simply has the appearance of flame.<br /> <br /> Fire immunity is by far the weakest investiture anyways, and I've never given it to an elder baali NPC (and had only one PC for whom it would be an character-appropriate investiture). The three dots of Fortitude that baali could have bought instead will handily soak most sources of fire damage on its own, and be a blanket protection against all other sources of aggravated to boot. Permanent flight, an analog to permanent zulo form (on a character with in-clan Obfuscate), access to any dark thaumaturgy path or ritual at-will -- or the holy grail, permanent immunity from frenzy of any type up to and including wassail itself -- have vastly more utility than mere fire immunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}